      "description": "Databases (DB) – a set of data that are organized according to certain rules (for example, a library is a database for books).\nDatabase management system (DBMS) is a software that allows you to create a database and manipulate it conveniently (perform various operations on the data). An example of a DBMS is a librarian. He can easily and efficiently work with the books in the library: give out requested books, take them back, add new ones, etc.",
